  "query_preview": "..\n/Issued 117 PM MDT Sun Sep 27 2026/ \n\n - Meteorological Overview:\n\nThis afternoon an upper-level ridge begins to build in over North-\ncentral, Central, and Southwestern Montana. This will keep cool \ntemperatures over the area. An upper-level shortwave will move \nthrough the upper-level flow this afternoon and evening and bring \nshowers and thunderstorms to Southwestern Montana. This evening \nisolated showers will spread to North-central Montana. On Monday a \nweak upper-level trough moves over North-central, Central, and \nSouthwestern Montana. This will bring showers and thunderstorms to \nSouthwestern Montana on Monday. It will warm up across the area with \nmostly dry weather north of I-90 on Monday.\n\nOn Tuesday there will be zonal (west to east) flow over North-\ncentral, Central, and Southwestern Montana. This will allow warm \ntemperatures to remain with dry weather. On Tuesday there will be \nstrong low-level and mid-level winds. This will bring windy \nconditions to North-central Montana with the strongest winds along\nthe Rocky Mountain Front. On Wednesday zonal flow remains over \nNorth-central, Central, and Southwestern Montana with strong low-\nlevel and mid-level winds. This will bring warm and mostly dry \nweather to the area with windy conditons across North-central \nMontana. On Thursday and Friday an upper-level ridge builds in \nover North-central, Central, and Southwestern Montana. This will \nallow temperatures to warm up with mostly dry weather across the \narea. -IG\n\n\n - Forecast Confidence & Scenarios:\n\nOn Monday there is a 20 - 30% chance for thunderstorms across \nsouthern Gallatin and Madison Counties. On Monday there is a 40 - \n60% chance for a quarter inch of rain or greater in the West \nYellowstone area. On Tuesday across the Northern Rocky Mountain \nFront there is a 40 - 70% chance for wind gusts of 75 mph or \ngreater. On Tuesday across the plains west of I-15 there is a a 20 - \n50% chance for wind gusts of 55 mph or greater. As a result a High \nWind Watch was issued for the northern Rocky Mountain Front and \nnorthern High Plains from 12 AM Tuesday to 12 AM Wednesday. -IG",
